WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
I've been making money outside a

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:05.800
traditional job for the last 24 years.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.840
Those extra income streams have helped

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.200
build a life of time freedom and

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.920
financial flexibility I always dreamed

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.560
about. Along the way, I started

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.320
interviewing other side hustlers about

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.720
their journey. Those interviews have

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.440
been downloaded over 35 million times

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.480
and have helped hundreds of thousands of

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.960
people take action and start their own

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.600
side hustle.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.080
Here's what I wish someone told me when

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.240
I was starting out.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.880
A lot of people approach side hustles

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.880
from the standpoint of I want to make

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.440
extra money. But what you need to do is

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.400
put yourself in the shoes of that

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.480
annoyingly curious 5-year-old and ask

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.040
why. And then ask why again. Why do you

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.520
want to make extra money? Well, I need a

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.760
little extra breathing room in my

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.360
budget. That would make life a little

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.600
more comfortable. Why? What do you want

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.840
to do? Well, I want to pay off some

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.200
debt. I want to maybe go on this family

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.080
trip. Why? Well, maybe eventually I want

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.840
to be able to quit my job and be in more

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.040
control of my calendar. Why? Well, I

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.120
really value having autonomy over my

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.680
time. And you start to drill down and

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.800
you get more and more honest with

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.480
yourself on why it's important to you.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.480
What do you really want and value

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.200
because this is going to keep you going

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.400
when times get tough in your side

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.480
hustle. It's like you see, it's hard. If

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.120
it were easy, everybody would be doing

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:18.480
it. And I think it's really important to

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.800
know that driving motivation, otherwise

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:23.000
it's too easy to throw in the towel. And

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.200
when you find a side hustle idea that

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.920
strikes your fancy, that is really

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.320
inspiring, you got to understand that

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.240
inspiration is temporary. So, do

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:33.600
everything you can to build some

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:36.480
positive momentum as quickly as you can

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.560
before that inspiration expires. Maybe

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.080
that's registering that domain name.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.520
Maybe that is making an offer. Maybe

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.840
that is putting a product up for sale.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.120
Whatever it is, like taking important

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.680
action because I think you'll find

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.080
momentum breeds momentum and momentum

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.800
breeds results and results is a virtuous

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.560
cycle in that way. And so, just

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.920
recognize inspiration has an expiration

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.440
date. And if you can take action before

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.880
then, I think you're going to be quite a

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.400
bit better off. And if you don't take

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.920
action in time, also recognize, look,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.640
business ideas are like buses. This is

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.880
the Richard Branson line. There's always

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.280
another one coming along. So, don't

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.640
stress if you missed the boat on one

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.360
because there's always something else

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.960
coming along. When it comes to coming up

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.520
with business ideas in the first place,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:20.400
you got to ask yourself, what are you

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:23.440
obsessed with? And the reason I bring

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.160
this up is it's hard to compete with

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.440
somebody who's obsessed. And I'll give

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.240
the example of credit card points and

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.880
miles. I like playing this game. I like

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.400
signing up for new credit card bonuses.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.720
Traveling for free is a fun little life

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:37.640
hack. But if I were to compete in this

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.200
space as a content creator, I'm never

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.600
going to compete with the points guy

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.000
with all the hacks, the people who

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:45.480
really live and breathe this stuff day

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.880
in and day out. Now, what I can compete,

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.360
what I have been obsessed with for the

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:50.960
last decade plus, is side hustle ideas,

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.840
right? This was the same questions that

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.840
I asked early on. What do you never get

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.680
tired of talking about? I really love

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.720
deconstructing these business ideas and

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.920
finding and sharing creative ways to

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.880
make extra money. Like that really

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:05.200
lights me up and it still does today the

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.520
way it did 12, 13 years ago. There's a

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.880
lot of advice around following your

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.200
passion, but I would argue if you don't

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.600
have something you're undyingly

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.560
passionate about and going back to the

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.560
obsession thing, maybe you can follow

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.760
your curiosity because this is what

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.040
drives a lot of the content in my case

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.160
as well. I'm curious. What would happen

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.520
if we tested this? Or what would happen

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:27.040
if we did this experiment? Like one

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:30.880
example, just recently I put the list in

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:33.040
episode that was generated by AI and it

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:34.280
was universally panned. The audience

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.640
didn't love it. I thought it was super

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:38.680
cool. I was excited by it. I found these

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:40.880
side hustle case studies and stories,

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.920
fed it into Notebook LM. It came back

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.880
with this cool like 17-minute back and

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.520
forth.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.480
It was an experiment. The crowd has

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.840
spoken. It wasn't It wasn't a winner.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.600
So, back to the drawing board on that.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.200
But it was something I was curious to

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.160
play around with. If you can follow your

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.320
curiosity and kind of be testing

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:59.720
different things. I read at one point

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.720
that Amazon is testing at any given

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.920
point like a thousand different

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.000
variables on their website trying to eke

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:07.760
out another point 01% conversion rate or

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.360
something because at their scale and

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.120
volume, that would be a significant bump

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.880
to the bottom line. Every little micro

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:16.560
percentage. I don't think you need to go

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:18.760
to that extreme, but you can run these

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.880
little experiments, these tests in your

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:23.200
day-to-day life. What would happen if I

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.240
did this? And it kind of gives yourself

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.760
permission to take a swing and say, oh,

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.600
if it don't work, it was just an

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:30.920
experiment. And similarly, I had to shut

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.920
down my Facebook content monetization

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.320
experiment last month just cuz it was

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:36.680
like, for the time that I'm putting into

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.600
this, the results aren't what I would be

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.200
hoping to get out. And it's okay. Hey,

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.080
you gave it an honest try. You gave it

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.560
the experiment. It didn't work. It was

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.240
following that curiosity. If I ever come

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.280
around with coming up with a kids book,

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.680
it would be, "Mommy, where do business

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:52.680
ideas come from?" And the truth is that

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.720
business ideas or money comes from

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.120
solving problems, right? A business is

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.960
just a repeatable system for solving a

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.480
problem. So, if you can put yourself in

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:03.560
that mindset, like early on, I probably

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:06.440
googled like a lot of us have, ways to

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:08.360
make money online. And what a lot of

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.280
these listicles that you find, and I've

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:13.040
written some of them myself,

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.840
dance around the issue of the real money

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.480
comes from solving problems. And I

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.520
stumbled into that with my first side

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:20.440
hustle or my first online side hustle

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:23.840
was this comparison shopping site for

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:25.320
shoes where the It was It started for

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.600
the noble purpose of how do I make money

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:30.840
online? But the end result was it was a

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:33.120
helpful tool, a helpful website to help

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:35.160
people find the best price on their next

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.520
pair of shoes. And that's why it worked.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:38.880
So, money comes from solving problems.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.080
Another thing we talk about quite a bit

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.920
on the show is the idea of pain pills

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:45.600
versus vitamins. And I think it is quite

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.080
a bit easier to sell pain pills than it

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.120
is to sell a vitamin. Cuz if you think

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:50.320
you've got this splitting headache,

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.920
you're going for the Excedrin, you're

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.640
going for the Tylenol right away.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:55.480
Versus, hey, if I forget to take my

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.680
vitamin today, it's probably not the end

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.840
of the world. What's that expensive

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.320
problem? What's that driving pain that

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:03.080
you can take away from customers and

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.640
solve that kind of problem? Early on, a

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.440
friend of mine gave me this line. He

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.160
called it the rule of the internet. He

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.320
said, "People are only ever online for

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.960
one of two reasons. Number one, to solve

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.440
a problem. Boom. I think that's easier

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:16.160
to play in. And number two, to be

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.520
entertained." And if you are very

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.560
entertaining, you can still play in in

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.680
that space. But you're competing against

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:25.000
Mr. Beast and ESPN and HBO and like all

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.320
of this stuff. Versus if you can solve a

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.600
very specific problem for a very

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.360
specific customer, I think it'll be much

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.760
easier to find an audience to start

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.760
making money that way. One thing that

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:36.000
comes up a lot is the idea of

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:38.280
competition. Somebody else is already

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.320
doing my idea. Somebody else already

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:42.400
came up with it. Somebody did it first.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:44.000
And so, Jonathan Mendonsa from ChooseFI

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.680
gave me this line on the show. He said,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.960
"If you can't be first, be different."

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.760
In his case, he was talking about the

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.080
financial independence movement, early

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.520
retirement. He said, "Look, there were

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.560
already dozens of blogs talking about

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:56.000
this. But there were very few podcasts.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:58.080
And so, ChooseFI filled that podcast

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.680
void for that early retirement

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.560
community. And I'll add the corollary to

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:04.880
that. If you can't be different, be

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.440
better, right? This is how the internet

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:08.800
overall improves in quality hopefully

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.720
over time because somebody else had the

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:12.160
same idea, but I can do it better. I can

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.840
kind of leapfrog what's already been

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.480
created. And you see this in physical

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.160
products all the time where it's Oh,

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:20.000
this already exists. Shoot. But here are

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:22.240
some little tweaks, little improvements,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:24.560
little iterations that we can make to

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:25.760
that to improve it over time. And I've

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.080
done the same thing with website

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.680
articles. Oh, shoot. Somebody already

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:31.240
wrote this idea. Now, back to the

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:34.120
drawing board. But Wait, I can still add

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:35.760
my own unique approach to this. I can be

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:38.280
different. I can hopefully be better.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.840
So, if you can't be first, be different.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:41.640
If you can't be different, be better.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.600
There's this proverb that talks about

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:46.000
when it comes to chasing a business

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.920
ideas about this lion on the African

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.520
savanna. It says it could either spend

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.880
its time chasing antelopes or chasing

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.560
mice. It's going to take the same amount

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.000
of effort either way. One is going to

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.760
feed him for a week. The other he's

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.000
going to still be hungry afterwards. And

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.680
so, I wanted you to think about this

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.320
when you're evaluating different

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:03.760
opportunities, different business ideas.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:06.040
Are you going after the antelope idea or

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:07.720
you going after the mouse idea? Like

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.560
even if you were If you succeed, if you

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.880
catch the thing, is that really going to

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:14.840
be worth your time? So, the question is,

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:17.800
what if this works? We spend a lot of

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:20.320
time talking about we have to minimize

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:23.040
failure, minimize risk. And I think all

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:25.800
of that is important. But you also have

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:28.760
to ask yourself, what if it works? And

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:30.320
if it does, would that be a win for you?

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:32.840
And the way to do that is to look at

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:35.159
somebody who's done it before you, who's

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:37.039
three or five years ahead of you and

00:08:35.159 --> 00:08:39.159
say, "What does their life look like

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:41.000
day-to-day? Are they still putting in

00:08:39.159 --> 00:08:43.080
80-hour workweeks? Or do they have a

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.360
little more freedom and flexibility? Is

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.720
their income where you would want it to

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:49.520
be?" You evaluate different side hustle

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:52.720
options based on what if it works? What

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:55.480
if the thing takes off and is that going

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:58.000
to be a win for me? The idea here is to

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:59.840
make an asymmetric bet or several

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.640
asymmetric bets because the first thing

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:04.240
that you try may not work and that's

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:06.520
okay. But if I minimize my downside risk

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:08.440
and swing for the big enough antelope or

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.160
the big enough upside, then that's going

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:12.240
to erase all my losses and I'm still

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:13.920
going to win. So, look at those side

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.320
hustles or those business ideas in terms

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.560
of what has an asymmetric upside. And I

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:20.600
think that's the side hustle mentality

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:23.800
in general. There's this connotation of

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:26.560
some entrepreneurial upside that

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:27.960
separates it from taking a second job,

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.480
bartending on the weekends, delivering

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:33.440
pizzas, driving for DoorDash, stuff like

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:36.240
that where Okay, there is a There's a

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.880
path here where I can go beyond hours

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:40.360
for dollars if I do this right. One

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:43.560
phrase that I have tried to remove from

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:44.800
my vocabulary is I don't have time or I

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.680
didn't have time. And what I've been

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.320
trying to replace that with is the more

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:51.040
brutally honest, I prioritized something

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:53.000
else. Because we vote our time with our

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:54.720
priorities. And we're all dealt the same

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:56.720
number of hours in the week. And your

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.080
week It look different from mine, but

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:59.480
there's some

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.600
level of truth to that. We have to look

